# Mobile-First Requirements

Design and implement for **320–767px first**, then enhance at `md:` (768px+).

## Breakpoint

- Mobile: `<768px` — use `useIsMobile()` or Tailwind `max-md:` / mobile-first `md:`
- Reference: `src/hooks/use-mobile.tsx`

## Checklist (every UI change)

- [ ] Layout OK at 320px width
- [ ] Touch targets ≥44×44px (buttons, links, toggles)
- [ ] No accidental horizontal page scroll
- [ ] Forms usable with on-screen keyboard
- [ ] Header/nav usable on touch (burger, mega menu)
- [ ] Desktop-only UI has mobile alternative (Sheet/Drawer, stack layout)

## Patterns in this repo

- Auth: `auth-styles.tsx` — single column under 600px
- Site chrome: `site-chrome.tsx` — responsive header
- Prefer shadcn `Sheet`/`Drawer` over hover-only desktop menus on mobile

Use skill `.cursor/skills/trenio-mobile-audit/` before finishing layout work.
